        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Pilgrim Hospital, Boston, Lincolnshire, England\n- Roads: A16, A52, Greenwich Meridian\n- Organizations: Boston High School\n- Topics: hospital location, school identity\n\nFacts:\n- Pilgrim Hospital is a large hospital in eastern Lincolnshire on the A16, north of the town of Boston near the mini-roundabout with the A52.\n- Pilgrim Hospital is situated virtually on the Greenwich Meridian and next to Boston High School.\n- Boston High School, also called Boston High School for Girls, is a selective grammar school and sixth form college for girls aged 11 to 18 in Boston, Lincolnshire, England.",
